usage: contractedge [-h]
                    {validate-input,prepare,prepare-benchmark,audit-release,run,repair,repair-batch,evaluate-repair-batch,evaluate-benchmark,evaluate,evaluate-cohort}
                    ...

ContractEdge frozen-benchmark planning, source repair and public feedback

positional arguments:
  {validate-input,prepare,prepare-benchmark,audit-release,run,repair,repair-batch,evaluate-repair-batch,evaluate-benchmark,evaluate,evaluate-cohort}
    validate-input      validate one MethodInput and its public Broken archive
    prepare             preflight/materialize manifest-listed isolated release
                        views
    prepare-benchmark   project the current frozen benchmark into public
                        MethodInputs
    audit-release       verify public/private hash manifests and isolation
    run                 run Requirement → Diagnosis → Semantic ChangeSet on a
                        public case
    repair              run the bounded public plan/patch/feedback loop on the
                        frozen benchmark
    repair-batch        resumable public repair cohort; independent hidden
                        scoring is separate
    evaluate-repair-batch
                        independent hidden scoring of frozen final batch
                        patches
    evaluate-benchmark  evaluator-only full150 GT/trace cohort accounting
    evaluate            score one trace in the evaluator-only process
    evaluate-cohort     score trace manifest against frozen evaluator
                        manifests, retaining all members

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
